Got you — here’s a **clean, exam-ready cheat sheet** with all the basic CLI templates you’ve been using (IP, RIP, OSPF, DHCP, NAT, Serial, etc.) 🚀
Keep this and you can solve almost any question.

---

#  1. BASIC ROUTER SETUP

```bash
enable
config t
hostname R1

interface g0/0
ip address <IP> <MASK>
no shutdown

interface s0/1/0
ip address <IP> <MASK>
clock rate 64000   ! only if DCE
no shutdown
```

---

#  2. STATIC ROUTING

```bash
ip route <destination-network> <mask> <next-hop-ip>
```

---

#  3. RIP (v2)

```bash
router rip
version 2
no auto-summary
network <major-network>
```

✅ Example:

```bash
network 192.168.1.0
```

---

#  4. OSPF

## Exact (subnet-wise)

```bash
router ospf 1
network <network> <wildcard> area 0
```

## Shortcut (covers all)

```bash
router ospf 1
network 192.168.1.0 0.0.0.255 area 0
```

---

#  5. DHCP

## Basic DHCP

```bash
ip dhcp excluded-address <start> <end>

ip dhcp pool <name>
network <network> <mask>
default-router <gateway>
dns-server 8.8.8.8
```

---

## Half DHCP + Half Static

```bash
ip dhcp excluded-address 192.168.1.1 192.168.1.50
```

👉 Manual: .1–.50
👉 DHCP: rest

---

# 🔥 6. NAT

## (A) Static NAT

```bash
interface g0/0
ip nat inside

interface s0/1/0
ip nat outside

ip nat inside source static <private-ip> <public-ip>
```

---

## (B) PAT (Overload) ⭐ MOST IMPORTANT

```bash
access-list 1 permit <network> <wildcard>

interface g0/0
ip nat inside

interface s0/1/0
ip nat outside

ip nat inside source list 1 interface s0/1/0 overload
```

---

# 🔥 7. RIP + OSPF (Redistribution)

```bash
router ospf 1
redistribute rip subnets

router rip
redistribute ospf 1 metric 1
```

---

# 🔥 8. VERIFY COMMANDS

```bash
show ip route
show ip interface brief
show ip nat translations
show ip dhcp binding
show ip ospf neighbor
```

